messages:
alex: Heads-up — I'm planning a small migration for analytics-worker: Deployment -> StatefulSet to keep the local PVC per replica. Change will also bump replicas 3 -> 4 and use a partitioned rolling update so we don't evict all pods at once. Putting the TF kube_manifest snippet here, want a quick sanity check before I apply.

alex: ```hcl
resource "kubernetes_manifest" "analytics_worker_sts" {
  manifest = {
    apiVersion = "apps/v1"
    kind       = "StatefulSet"
    metadata = { name = "analytics-worker" namespace = "prod" }
    spec = {
      replicas = 4
      selector = { matchLabels = { app = "analytics-worker" } }
      template = {
        metadata = { labels = { app = "analytics-worker" } }
        spec = { containers = [{ name = "worker", image = "ghcr.io/redwood/analytics-worker:v2", resources = { requests = { cpu = "250m", memory = "512Mi" }, limits = { cpu = "1000m", memory = "1Gi" } }, volumeMounts = [{ name = "data", mountPath = "/var/data" }] }], volumes = [] }
      }
      volumeClaimTemplates = [{ metadata = { name = "data" }, spec = { accessModes = ["ReadWriteOnce"], resources = { requests = { storage = "20Gi" } } } }]
      updateStrategy = { type = "RollingUpdate", rollingUpdate = { partition = 1 } }
    }
  }
}
```

priya: Quick q — are we keeping HPA on this? StatefulSets + HPA can be tricky unless we use External metrics or scale the headless service.

alex: Good call. No HPA for this workload for now — we're keeping it manually scaled because of the PVCs. I added a note in the PR to revisit with a migration to shared storage or CSI clones.

jamie: Two things: 1) If a pod restarts during rolling update we could briefly drop capacity. Can we set maxUnavailable = 0 (so we rely on partition and extra replica) and preStop to drain gracefully? 2) Make sure podTopologySpread / affinity stays the same so we don't pack all replicas on one AZ.

marta: Also verifying secrets — the new template keeps the same secretName for DB creds, right? We had a name change in the last TF pass and that caused a mount mismatch.

alex: Yes, secret name unchanged (analytics-db-creds). I ran `terraform plan -target=kubernetes_manifest.analytics_worker_sts` locally — plan looks clean, only the statefulset resource will update. Paste of the relevant plan lines: 

alex: ```
~ kubernetes_manifest.analytics_worker_sts
    spec: {
      + replicas: 4
      ~ updateStrategy.0.rollingUpdate.0.partition: 0 => 1
    }

Plan: 0 to add, 1 to change, 0 to destroy.
```

priya: LGTM, one nit: set maxUnavailable=0 like jamie suggested and maybe lower the probe timeout for readiness to avoid slow starts blocking rollouts.

jamie: Agree. Also leave a canary namespace apply first (prod-canary) and let deploybot run health checks for 10m. If all good, roll to prod.

alex: Will do canary apply first. Scheduling at 03:15 UTC (low traffic). Pinging @oncall and tagging the PR in #eng-releases.

sre-bot: deploybot: plan for analytics-worker (prod-canary) successful — no diffs besides StatefulSet update. CI checks passed.

marta: :thumbsup: From security/secrets side this looks fine.

priya: :eyes: I'll be around for the 03:15 window to watch metrics.

alex: Thanks all — I'll apply the canary and post the rollout snippet when it's live.``
